{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1114,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Dan.5","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Daniel","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Daniel 5","reference":"Daniel 5","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Belshazzar's profane feast, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-4.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The hand writing on the wall, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"5-9.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Interpreted and applied by Daniel, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"10-29.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"The accomplishment of it, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"30, 31.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"Belshazzar - The grandson of Nebuchadnezzar.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":11,"text":"Made a great feast - After the manner of the eastern kings who shewed their magnificence this way.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":12,"text":"But this is prodigious that he should carouse when the city was besieged, and ready to be taken by Darius the Mede.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":13,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":14,"text":"To bring the vessels - Triumphing thereby over God and his people.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":15,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":16,"text":"And praised the gods of gold - At the same time insulting the great God of heaven and earth.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":17,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"Came forth fingers - The likeness of a man's hand.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":20,"text":"His knees smote - So soon can the terrors of God make the loftiest cedars, the tyrants of the earth.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":21,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":22,"text":"The queen came - The women in those courts had an apartment by themselves, and this being the queen-mother, and aged, did not mingle herself with the king's wives and concubines, yet she broke the rule in coming in now, upon this solemn occasion.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":23,"text":"24.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":24,"text":"From him - From that God whom thou hast despised.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":25,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":26,"text":"MENE - MENE MENE, it is numbered, it is numbered; the words are doubled for the greater confirmation.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":27,"text":"It relates to the number of the seventy years for the overthrow of the Babylonish empire.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":28,"text":"27.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":29,"text":"Art found wanting - There is no weight nor worth in thee; thou hast made light of God, and the Lord makes light of thee.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":30,"text":"28.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":31,"text":"PERES - Separated, divided, broken.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":32,"text":"Phars signifies two things, broken off, and Persian; noting that, first, this kingdom was broken down from Belshazzar.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":33,"text":"Secondly, that it was given to the Persians.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":34,"text":"31.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":31,"scriptureVerseEnd":31},{"verse":35,"text":"Darius the Mede - This was he that with Cyrus besieged and took Babylon.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":31,"scriptureVerseEnd":31}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Daniel","chapter":5}}